<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Idwal Foel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/942">942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Idwal Foel, meaning 'the bald', was king of Gwynedd from 916 to 942, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodri-the-great">Rhodri the Great</a>. He submitted to the English kings and attended the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelstan">Æthelstan</a>, witnessing his charters. In 942 he was killed fighting the English, and his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hywel-dda">Hywel Dda</a> of Deheubarth seized Gwynedd, excluding his sons until Hywel's death in 950.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/idwal-foel.jpg" alt="Idwal Foel" width="320" height="288" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Powell and Humphrey Lloyd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Idwalfoel_historieofcambria.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
